<title>AUSTRALIA: Comalco aluminium output up in half year.</title>
<headline>Comalco aluminium output up in half year.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Comalco Ltd said on Wednesday that its primary aluminium production rose to 254,737 tonnes in the half year to June 30 from 225,477 tonnes a year earlier.  </p>
<p>Comalco said its bauxite production rose to 172,123 tonnes in the first half from 168,851 tonnes a year earlier.</p>
<p>&quot;Higher aluminium production is due to new cells coming on line as part of the startup of line three at the Boyne Island smelter (Queensland) and the upgrade at the Tiwai Point smelter in New Zealand,&quot; Comalco said.</p>
<p>The company said bauxite production at Weipa, Queensland, was affected by heavy rains in the first quarter of 1997.  </p>
